```dafny
method ToArray<T>(xs: seq<T>) returns (a: array<T>)
  requires |xs| > 0
  ensures fresh(a)
  ensures a.Length == |xs|
  ensures forall i :: 0 <= i < a.Length ==> a[i] == xs[i]
{
  a := new T[|xs|];
  
  var i := 0;
  while i < a.Length
    invariant 0 <= i <= a.Length
    invariant forall j :: 0 <= j < i ==> a[j] == xs[j]
  {
    a[i] := xs[i];
    i := i + 1;
  }
}
```

**Explanation:**
- **Fresh Allocation**: `new T[|xs|]` ensures a fresh array allocation
- **Length Match**: `a.Length == |xs|` is guaranteed by construction
- **Content Preservation**: The loop invariant ensures each element matches the sequence
- **Verification**: The loop invariant is sufficient for Dafny to verify the postconditions
- **Clean Design**: No unnecessary complexity, follows straightforward array initialization pattern
- **Type Safety**: Generic `T` preserves type safety while being reusable

The implementation directly satisfies all requirements with minimal complexity and optimal verification performance.
